  "content": {
    "id": "p19-q40-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": "State the axis in which $y=x^2(x-2)^2$ was reflected to give $y=-x^2(2-x)^2$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "The $x$-axis.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y&=-x^2\\bigl(-(x-2)\\bigr)^2\\\\y&=-x^2(x-2)^2.\\end{align*}$$\nThe new output is the negative of the original output, so the graph was reflected in the $x$-axis.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
